(III)--a son of ब्रह्मा, born of the right side of his chest; one of the first five created things for the propagation of people; the first devata who married the thirteen daughters of दक्ष or the दाक्षायणिस् (ten: वा। प्।): each of whom had sons; they were श्रद्धा, लक्ष्मी, धृति, तुष्टि, पुष्टि, मेधा, क्रिया, Buddhi, लज्जा, Vasu, शान्ति, Siddhi and कीर्ति;
1: भा. III. १२. २५; IV. I. ४८-50; Br. II. 9. 1, ४९-50; IV. 1. ४०; M. 3. १०; 4. ३४ and ५५; 5. १३; १४६. १६; Va. 1. ६९; १०. २६; १००. ४३; Vi. I. 7. २४, २८-31; १५. ७७, १०३. वा. ६३. ४१; ६६. 2; ७६. 3.
